.Dd November 12, 2026
.Dt ICONV 3
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm iconv ,
.Nm iconv_open ,
.Nm iconv_close
.Nd character-set conversion
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In iconv.h
.Ft iconv_t
.Fn iconv_open "const char *tocode" "const char *fromcode"
.Ft size_t
.Fn iconv "iconv_t cd" "char **inbuf" "size_t *inbytesleft" "char **outbuf" "size_t *outbytesleft"
.Ft int
.Fn iconv_close "iconv_t cd"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The iconv family converts a byte stream between character sets.
The converter keeps its partial-input state in the descriptor returned by .Fn iconv_open.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn iconv_open returns a descriptor or .Dv (iconv_t)-1. .Fn iconv returns the number of
non-reversible conversions or .Dv (size_t)-1. .Fn iconv_close returns 0 or -1.
.Sh ERRORS
.Er EINVAL is returned for an unsupported target encoding or an incomplete input sequence.
.Er E2BIG is returned when the output buffer is full.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr locale 7
.Sh STANDARDS
POSIX.1-2024; ring 0.
.Sh CAVEATS
CJK charsets are decode-only.
Using one as a target fails with .Er EINVAL.
See H-8 and C48.
